        "biography": "Renowned Music Producer and Supervisor for musicals films, Matt Sullivan has garnered multiple Grammy nominations for his exceptional work. To date, he has overseen the production of an unprecedented sixteen musicals films. Sullivan collaborates closely with directors on set and in the recording studio, guiding and overseeing the film's musical direction. This includes the song and score arrangements, orchestrations, recording, and mixing. Sullivan's unique process involves meticulous collaboration with actors in the studio and on set to capture not only robust singing performances but also performances that resonate with the character's essence. His ability to balance technical expertise with deep creative collaboration has made him an integral part of the success of some of the most iconic musical films. He has work alongside many exceptional Director's among them, Bill Condon, Steven Spielberg, Robert Zemeckis, Rob Marshall, Guy Ritchie and Adam Shankman. His work has contributed to the success of films including West Side Story, Aladdin, Beauty and the Beast, Begin Again, Rock of Ages, Hairspray, Dreamgirls, Rent, Nine, and Chicago, with many of the soundtracks and songs earning Academy Award and Grammy nominations and wins.",
